--- a/baseline/orchestrarium-v1/README.md
+++ b/baseline/orchestrarium-v1/README.md
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ The verifier performs the operational work rather than duplicating security-sens
 - validates the complete consumed `baseline-pin.json` shape before orchestration, so malformed evidence exits operationally with code `2` rather than raising an uncaught key lookup;
 - treats path, content digest, Git mode, and Git object type as capability identity, so executable-bit and symbolic-link changes cannot disappear behind unchanged file bytes;
 - requires a schema-version-2 disposition envelope whose direct-parent candidate commit and exact content digest, Git mode, and Git object type match every approved added or modified path; the final reviewed commit may change only the envelope itself;
-- compares Pytest exits, JUnit Extensible Markup Language diagnostics, retained skip reasons, and baseline test/support source digests;
+- disables Pytest's cache provider so a test lane cannot create or consume repository-local `.scratch/pytest-cache`, then compares exits, JUnit Extensible Markup Language diagnostics, retained skip reasons, and baseline test/support source digests;
 - runs all repository-standard validators in both worktrees and requires validator-specific terminal success or failure markers even when both commands exit zero;
 - rechecks both baseline and candidate worktrees after every untrusted repository-code stage, including each candidate-focused test suite;
 - snapshots the complete trusted-tree membership and identity before each untrusted lane, forbids new entries, removals, replacements, symbolic links, hard links, or special files, and verifies the exact tree afterward;
